        "Persistence actions checked successful import, deletion, and capture with separate reloads: IDs/order/values/angles survived while live scene restarted at 0 s, 1x, no selection, overview, and automatic playback. Corrupting only this artifact storage key then reloading yielded an empty list and visible recovery notice; seek/selection controls remained usable and valid export was re-imported. A page-local injected QuotaExceededError on Storage.prototype.setItem exercised saving failure: visible saving-unavailable warning, third snapshot remained usable in memory, prior persisted list stayed at two, and live state stayed exact. The original method was restored and valid data saved again. Genuine browser-disabled storage/read-unavailable conditions were not exercised.",
        "Viewport/keyboard method: top-level setViewportSize returned TypeError: not a function. A temporary same-origin iframe created only in an owned tab DOM provided real contentWindow viewports 1440x900 and 390x844, loading unchanged index.html. At both sizes screenshots and measured bounds showed no horizontal overflow or out-of-width primary controls. Actual Tab/Shift+Tab, Enter, Home/ArrowRight range changes, number typing/ArrowUp, and textarea typing exercised selection, pause/resume, seeking, speed, tracking/overview, capture/restore/delete, export/import. Focus-visible outlines were observed and Tab left/re-entered controls without a trap. All three planets were also clicked on the canvas at both sizes; paused overview drag/wheel zoom changed perspective without selection, and null overview restore reproduced framing exactly.",
